From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justinas Grauslis <justinas@8devices.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix commit of an uninitialised gpt_disk

update_slot_attribute() opens each partition's disk lazily, and flushes the
disk it already holds when the next partition turns out to live on a different
one. On the first iteration there is no disk held yet: the struct is still the
zeroed one from the caller, partition_is_for_disk() compares against an empty
devpath and returns false, and the code commits a disk that was never read.
gpt_disk_commit() rejects it:

  gpt_disk_commit: Invalid args
  update_slot_attribute: Failed to commit disk
  SLOT a: Failed to set as unbootable

Whether this is reached depends only on what the caller happened to do first.
mark_boot_successful() and set_active_boot_slot() read attributes before they
write, and those reads initialise the struct, so they work. set_slot_as_
unbootable() goes straight to update_slot_attribute() with a zeroed struct, so
qbootctl -u can never succeed.

Skip the flush when no disk is held yet. "Nothing to commit" is the normal
state of the first iteration, not a failure, and gpt-utils already exports
gpt_disk_is_valid() for the test.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 bootctrl_impl.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bootctrl_impl.c b/bootctrl_impl.c
--- a/bootctrl_impl.c
+++ b/bootctrl_impl.c
@@ -212,8 +212,10 @@
 		LOGD("%s: partName = '%s'\n", __func__, partName);
 
 		// If the current partition is for a different disk (e.g. /dev/sde when the current disk is /dev/sda)
-		// Then commit the current disk
-		if (!partition_is_for_disk(disk, partName, devpath, sizeof(devpath))) {
+		// Then commit the current disk. Nothing is held on the first
+		// iteration, and committing a disk that was never read fails.
+		if (gpt_disk_is_valid(disk) &&
+		    !partition_is_for_disk(disk, partName, devpath, sizeof(devpath))) {
 			if (gpt_disk_commit(disk)) {
 				fprintf(stderr, "%s: Failed to commit disk\n", __func__);
 				return -1;
